TEXT -408 504 Left 2 ;r_x = relation between ohmic and inductive part of the coil\nr_x = 0.03 * xd\nxd = delta_un*v/sqrt(3)/in or xd = delta_un*v*v/Sd\nin * xd [V] = ud * v ->  voltage across xd
TEXT -408 456 Left 2 ;Formulas:\nxd = delta_un * v*v / Sd        ( Sd = sqrt(3) * v*in )
TEXT -400 240 Left 2 ;nominal values for ud : 0.03 - 0.05 - 0.06 - 0.08 - 0.1
TEXT -400 256 Left 2 ;nominal values for "in" : 160A - 250A - 400A - 630A -\n    - 1000A - 1600A - 2500A
TEXT -400 224 Left 2 ;delta_un [ %] = ud * 100 -> percentage of v ( across xd )
TEXT -408 568 Left 2 ;xd = 0.1 * 10000 / 1,732 / 250 = 2.309 ohm\nin * xd = 250 * 2.309 = 577V  =>   0.1 * ( 10000/sqrt(3) )
TEXT -32 112 Left 2 ;Example with a current limiting reactor on a line_LF\nnormal load (no fault) case
